  "title": "Journal v2: schema-validated, indexed, replayable run journals",
  "summary": "The checkpoint runner's journal grows from a two-payload buffer into a versioned event log. Events now carry a typed actor, work item, change and cost; every event is validated against a JSON Schema before a byte is written; the chain hash covers the decision fields while a separate replay digest proves a replay; and each work item gets a lock-protected index of its runs. The buffer directory is renamed to runs, and a reader replays and verifies a journal end to end.",
  "lenses": [
    "architecture",
    "data-flow"
  ],
